"/arc-plc/south-carolina/sumter-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 10 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and October to November came in under 90% of normal in 39 of 75 years, more than any other pair. In 2025 that pair hit 129% of normal, while January to February sat at 50%. So far in 2026, March to April came in at 23% of normal on the middle of the grids. Every grid had its driest year in 1954, with grid 16398 at 53%.</p>"}
